From 5bc3068e1cbc13e5725bb4249ecc679795635c0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 11:34:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dflash: ingest buun's DFlash2 adaptive controller - built,
 gated, and defaulted OFF by measurement

The President approved ingesting buun's DFlash2 work on the expectation it carried both a prose-
collapse fix and a speed gain. It was ingested properly rather than assessed and set aside. It does
not earn the default, and the reason it does not is worth more than the code.

WHAT LANDED, semantically integrated against our independently diverged tree, not cherry-picked:
  - the adaptive controller and its per-sequence state (common/speculative.cpp)
  - the 8 -> 13 block-size metadata mapping (src/models/dflash.cpp)
  - a DFlash2 pre-flight that sizes draft.n_max before target context creation (server-context.cpp)
  - explicit-depth tracking so an operator's --spec-draft-n-max is never silently overridden
Nothing under ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ is touched, so the escha kernel work is untouched. Upstream's
dotted tensor-name aliases were NOT taken; the analogalok sidecar loads without them.

THE GATE. 16 prompts weighted to prose, depth 7 as a positive control, every arm scored for
degeneration - empty output, repeated n-gram, prompt echo - beside throughput:
    plain               3.91 t/s   clean
    fixed cap 3         6.59 t/s   clean            <- incumbent, and the winner
    reactive (buun)     4.04 t/s   8 of 16 degenerate
    preventive (ours)   4.20 t/s   9 of 16 degenerate
    control depth 7     5.36 t/s   8 of 16 degenerate
    mtp self-draft      6.56 t/s   clean
Both controllers are slower AND broken, so defaulting them off trades nothing away.

WHY THEY FAIL. Both steer on draft ACCEPTANCE, and acceptance does not track output quality on this
model: the clean fixed-cap arm runs at 0.67-0.77 acceptance while the preventive arm scored a
perfect 1.00 on a task inside a run that degenerated on 9 of 16 prompts. An acceptance-driven
controller climbs into the broken region precisely because everything looks perfect to it. The
preventive variant starts at depth 2 - a depth measured clean - and degenerates anyway, which is
that mechanism caught in the act. A controller that works here must steer on an output-degeneration
signal; until one exists a hard depth cap is the honest control.

Both policies stay reachable behind GGML_DFLASH2_ADAPTIVE and GGML_DFLASH2_PREVENTIVE with the
numbers recorded at the switch, because on a model whose acceptance does track quality they may
well win - and re-deriving this would cost another rig day.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native), integrating github.com/spiritbuun/buun-llama-cpp 396469835..1ab12e269
